<div class="overlay" id="scoreHelp" hidden>
  <div class="panel light">
    <h2>How towers score</h2><p><b>Roll odds:</b> ordinary rolls have a 15% triple, 55% pair, and 30% no-match chance. Every roll throws all three dice; dice locking and combat rerolls are removed. HOT and Shadowstrike apply their stated bonuses. Paid war rolls grant 1 XP per energy actually spent; gold is currency only and no longer grants XP.</p>
    <p><b>Shields:</b> three slots per hero. Each shield absorbs a base sword-pair hit, scaled by its earning multiplier. Stronger shields replace the weakest; excess damage carries through.</p><p><b>War rewards:</b> make at least 5 paid rolls during the daily war. Completion energy is limited to 20 daily; the final push also has a separate 30-energy rally gift, once per day. Rampage never recharges itself, and ultimate charge is capped at 10 per roll.</p>
    <p><b class="blue">Damage decides it.</b> Every hit your guild lands at a tower — on the garrison, or on the tower itself once the garrison is wiped — adds to your damage total there. The guild with the higher total <b>holds</b> the tower. A tie holds for nobody.</p>
    <p><b class="gold">Held towers are your score.</b> Courtyard towers are worth 3♛, camp towers 2♛, outposts 1♛. Daytime control counts: your average held tower points are banked. At the finish, add twice the points of the towers you hold. Highest total wins; guild damage breaks a tie. The last 30 minutes boost attack damage ×1.5.</p>
    <p><b class="orange">Siege.</b> When every defender at a tower is down, the knockout that wipes them <b>breaches</b> the tower (a chunk of tower damage banked instantly), and your rolls then hit the tower's score directly at <b>120%</b> — undefended walls — until someone respawns. No KOs or loot during a siege, but it's the fastest scoring in the game, so clear garrisons and pile on.</p>
    <button class="go green" id="shOk">GOT IT</button>
  </div>
